Subject: libretro: load a queued cart before restoring a save state
Origin: Korri (local patch, not part of upstream PR #288)
Upstream-status: Not submitted
Applies-after: eris-save-states.patch (PR #288)

retro_load_game only queues the cart. RetroArch's savestate_auto_load calls
retro_unserialize before the first retro_run, so Step later loads the cart,
resets RAM/Lua and discards the restore. Extract Step's existing queue
processing and call it before restoring, without ticking the previous cart.
Normal Step loading still uses the same implementation.

Regression: save-state-check.c runs PR #288's savestatetest.p8, saves at
Lua counter 30, then in a fresh process loads/restores before any retro_run.
PR #288 alone yields counters 31 then 1 (expected 31 then 32). The running,
fresh auto-load and unload/reload cases must all yield 31, 32, 33, for both
memory-backed and path-backed loads. This patch changes no state format.

--- a/source/vm.cpp
+++ b/source/vm.cpp
@@ -638,6 +638,11 @@
     }
     lua_pop(_luaState, 1);
 
+    ProcessQueuedCartChange();
+    return ret;
+}
+
+void Vm::ProcessQueuedCartChange(){
     // Process any queued cart change (from reset, load, etc.)
     if (_cartChangeQueued) {
         Logger_Write("Processing cart change, _pauseMenu = %s\n", _pauseMenu ? "true" : "false");
@@ -660,8 +665,6 @@
             _cartChangeQueued = false;
         }
     }
-
-    return ret;
 }
 
 // void Vm::UpdateAndDraw() {
--- a/source/vm.h
+++ b/source/vm.h
@@ -79,6 +79,7 @@
 
     // void UpdateAndDraw();
     bool Step();
+    void ProcessQueuedCartChange();
 
     uint8_t* GetPicoInteralFb();
     uint8_t* GetScreenPaletteMap();
--- a/platform/libretro/libretro.cpp
+++ b/platform/libretro/libretro.cpp
@@ -657,6 +657,12 @@
 
 EXPORT bool retro_unserialize(const void *data, size_t size)
 {
+    // RetroArch auto-loads states after retro_load_game, before retro_run.
+    // Finish the queued load (including vm_run) first: it resets RAM and Lua
+    // and would otherwise overwrite the restored state on the next frame.
+    // Do not tick the old cart or submit a frontend video/audio frame here.
+    _vm->ProcessQueuedCartChange();
+
     if (log_cb) {
         log_cb(RETRO_LOG_INFO, "lua deserialize\n");
     }
